tile (B7) for a potentially more dangerous later turn, or to discard B2 simply to clear the hand.\n\nReason: The hand is aiming for an 8-point structure relying on drawing B3 to complete a Mixed Double Chow and All Simples hand. B2 and B7 are useless for this specific high-scoring configuration. Since B7 is a completely safe tile (all 4 accounted for), it is better to discard B2 first (which is safe but theoretically less so) or simply discard B2 to clear the path for the B3 wait, as B234 results in a non-winning hand value.\n\nAnswer: Play B2"}
